---
import trustpointLogo from "../img/trustpoint_labs_logo.svg?url";
import trustpointFavicon from "../img/trustpoint_favicon.png?url";

import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/400.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/500.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/600.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/700.css";

import "../styles/global.css";

const githubUrl = "https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />

    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    />

    <title>
      Industrial PKI & Trustpoint Services | Trustpoint Labs
    </title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Industrial PKI and machine identity management for OT. Trustpoint Labs helps you deploy, integrate and support the open-source Trustpoint platform."
    />

    <meta
      name="robots"
      content="index, follow"
    />

    <link
      rel="canonical"
      href="https://trustpoint-labs.com/"
    />

    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href={trustpointFavicon}
    />

    <link
      rel="apple-touch-icon"
      sizes="180x180"
      href="/apple-touch-icon.png"
    />

    <meta name="theme-color" content="#004aad" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />

    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "Trustpoint Labs",
      url: "https://trustpoint-labs.com/",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project"],
      description: "Professional services for Trustpoint, the open-source industrial PKI and machine identity management platform: OT deployment, integration, engineering and support."
    })} />

    <!-- Open Graph -->

    <meta
      property="og:type"
      content="website"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="Industrial PKI & Trustpoint Services | Trustpoint Labs"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Deploy industrial PKI in OT with Trustpoint. Engineering, integration, OEM solutions and professional support for machine identity and certificate management."
    />

    <meta
      property="og:url"
      content="https://trustpoint-labs.com/"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:site_name"
      content="Trustpoint Labs"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:image"
      content="https://trustpoint-labs.com/og-image.png"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:image:width"
      content="1200"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:image:height"
      content="630"
    />

    <meta
      property="og:image:alt"
      content="Trustpoint Labs – Industrial PKI and Machine Identity Management"
    />

  </head>

  <body>

    <!-- ===================================
         HEADER
    ==================================== -->

    <header class="shell">

      <a
        class="logo-link"
        href="/"
        aria-label="Trustpoint Labs"
      >
        <img
          class="logo"
          src={trustpointLogo}
          alt="Trustpoint Labs"
          width="205"
          height="115"
        />
      </a>

      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">

        <a href="#offering">
          Offering
        </a>

        <a href="#why-trustpoint">
          Why Trustpoint
        </a>

        <a href="#open-source">
          Open Source
        </a>

        <a href="#contact">
          Contact
        </a>

        <a
          class="github"
          href={githubUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub
          <span>↗︎</span>
        </a>

      </nav>

    </header>


    <main>

      <!-- =================================
           HERO
      ================================== -->

      <section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-content shell">
    <div class="kicker"><span class="square"></span> INDUSTRIAL PKI · MACHINE IDENTITY · OT</div>
    <h1>Industrial PKI &amp; machine identity.<br /><span class="hero-accent">Powered by Trustpoint.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-description">Trustpoint is an open-source platform for industrial PKI, machine identity and certificate lifecycle management. Deploy it in OT networks to manage device certificates, automate enrollment and renewal, and integrate with your existing PKI. Trustpoint Labs provides the engineering, integration and professional support to make it work in your environment.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="#offering">Explore our services <span>↓︎</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="#trustpoint">What is Trustpoint? <span>→︎</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/use-cases/">Explore use cases <span>→︎</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-note">Open-source industrial PKI · Local OT deployment · Existing PKI integration</div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           PROBLEM / SOLUTION
      ================================== -->

      <section class="section shell" id="trustpoint">
  <div class="section-label"><span class="square"></span> WHAT IS TRUSTPOINT?</div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <h2>Certificate management, built for industrial OT.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Trustpoint manages certificate-based identities for industrial devices, machines and applications. It helps bring certificate issuance, renewal, revocation and trust relationships into a manageable lifecycle instead of scattered manual processes.</p>
      <p class="lede">Run Trustpoint locally in factory networks, close to your devices, or connect it to an existing enterprise CA through its registration authority capabilities. The platform is designed for segmented networks, limited connectivity and brownfield equipment. Trustpoint Labs helps you deploy and extend it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-index">01</span><div><h3>Machine identities</h3><p>Establish and manage certificate-based identities for industrial devices and machines.</p></div><span class="feature-glyph">+</span></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-index">02</span><div><h3>Certificate lifecycle</h3><p>Reduce manual work across enrollment, renewal and revocation workflows.</p></div><span class="feature-glyph">↔︎</span></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-index">03</span><div><h3>Industrial PKI integration</h3><p>Deploy Trustpoint as a local CA or connect OT systems to an existing enterprise PKI through its RA capabilities.</p></div><span class="feature-glyph">↗︎</span></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-index">04</span><div><h3>OT device onboarding</h3><p>Manage identities for industrial devices, including manual brownfield workflows and supported automated enrollment.</p></div><span class="feature-glyph">→︎</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           OFFERING
      ================================== -->

      <section class="offering section" id="offering">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="square"></span> OUR SERVICES</div>
    <div class="offering-heading">
      <h2>Professional services built around Trustpoint.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Deploy industrial PKI in OT with Trustpoint. We help you plan the architecture, connect devices and existing CAs, automate certificate lifecycles, build tailored integrations and support eligible Trustpoint releases.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-grid">
      <article class="offering-card">
        <span class="offering-index">01</span>
        <h3>Engineering &amp; Integration</h3>
        <p>Deploy and integrate Trustpoint in your industrial environment, from architecture and device onboarding to customer-specific engineering.</p>
        <ul><li>Trustpoint architecture &amp; deployment</li><li>Enterprise PKI and CA/RA integration</li><li>Device onboarding and certificate automation</li><li>OPC UA / GDS, CMP and EST workflows</li><li>Custom connectors, APIs and extensions</li></ul>
        <a href="/engineering-integration/" class="offering-link">Explore engineering services <span aria-hidden="true">→︎</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="offering-card">
        <span class="offering-index">02</span>
        <h3>Support &amp; Maintenance</h3>
        <p>Get contract-based break/fix support for eligible official Trustpoint releases, with a clearly defined scope and severity-based initial response targets.</p>
        <ul><li>Trustpoint troubleshooting and defect analysis</li><li>Certificate workflow and API diagnostics</li><li>Installation and configuration troubleshooting</li><li>Upgrade-related troubleshooting</li><li>Separately agreed maintenance when needed</li></ul>
        <a href="/support/" class="offering-link">View support scope <span aria-hidden="true">→︎</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="offering-card">
        <span class="offering-index">03</span>
        <h3>OEM &amp; White Label</h3>
        <p>Build on Trustpoint as a foundation for customer-specific products and industrial solutions, with engineering arrangements tailored to the project.</p>
        <ul><li>Trustpoint-based OEM integration</li><li>White-label development</li><li>Embedded or containerized deployments</li><li>Product-specific features and workflows</li><li>Individually agreed engineering and support</li></ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           WHY TRUSTPOINT
      ================================== -->

      <section class="highlight" id="why-trustpoint">
  <div class="highlight-inner shell">
    <div class="section-label section-label-light">WHY TRUSTPOINT</div>
    <div class="highlight-grid">
      <h2>Built for industrial OT.</h2>
      <p>Trustpoint brings industrial PKI and certificate lifecycle management into OT networks. As a locally deployable open-source platform, it connects machine identities, existing certificate authorities and industrial devices without relying on permanent cloud connectivity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="usp-grid">
      <article class="usp-item"><span>01</span><h3>Industrial PKI</h3><p>Manage device identities, certificate issuance, renewal and revocation in OT environments.</p></article>
      <article class="usp-item"><span>02</span><h3>Local &amp; offline-capable</h3><p>Deploy without permanent cloud connectivity; certificate issuance still requires a reachable CA in the relevant environment.</p></article>
      <article class="usp-item"><span>03</span><h3>Brownfield workflows</h3><p>Combine manual device onboarding with automation where devices and interfaces permit.</p></article>
      <article class="usp-item"><span>04</span><h3>Enrollment &amp; OPC UA</h3><p>Connect supported CMP, EST and OPC UA/GDS certificate workflows, subject to release and device capabilities.</p></article>
      <article class="usp-item"><span>05</span><h3>Open source</h3><p>Source code is publicly available for inspection, adaptation and contribution under its license.</p></article>
      <article class="usp-item"><span>06</span><h3>Existing PKI integration</h3><p>Use Trustpoint alongside existing PKI infrastructure rather than replacing it by default.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           HOW WE WORK
      ================================== -->

      <section class="section shell">
  <div class="section-label"><span class="square"></span> HOW WE WORK</div>
  <div class="process-heading"><h2>Assess. Integrate. Hand over.</h2></div>
  <div class="process-grid">
    <article class="process-item"><span class="process-index">01</span><h3>Assess &amp; design</h3><p>Review your Trustpoint use case, device landscape, existing PKI, network boundaries and project requirements.</p></article>
    <article class="process-item"><span class="process-index">02</span><h3>Implement &amp; validate</h3><p>Configure and integrate Trustpoint, develop agreed extensions and validate workflows against project-specific acceptance criteria.</p></article>
    <article class="process-item"><span class="process-index">03</span><h3>Hand over &amp; support</h3><p>Deliver documentation and operational guidance. Commercial break/fix support and further engineering are available through separate agreements; customers retain operational responsibility.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           DEPLOYMENT MODELS
      ================================== -->

      <section class="deployment section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="square"></span> TRUSTPOINT DEPLOYMENT SCENARIOS</div>
    <div class="deployment-heading"><h2>Deploy industrial PKI where it is needed.</h2></div>
    <div class="deployment-grid">
      <article class="deployment-card"><span>01</span><h3>Local OT Edge</h3><p>Run Trustpoint close to machines and devices inside industrial networks.</p></article>
      <article class="deployment-card"><span>02</span><h3>Registration Authority</h3><p>Connect OT certificate workflows to an existing issuing PKI through Trustpoint's RA capabilities.</p></article>
      <article class="deployment-card"><span>03</span><h3>Local CA</h3><p>Use local certificate issuance for suitable segmented or isolated environments.</p></article>
      <article class="deployment-card"><span>04</span><h3>OEM Integration</h3><p>Integrate Trustpoint into a customer-specific industrial product or software solution.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           OPEN SOURCE
      ================================== -->

      <section class="section shell" id="open-source">
  <div class="section-label"><span class="square"></span> OPEN SOURCE &amp; PROFESSIONAL SERVICES</div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div><h2>Open source at the core. Professional services around it.</h2></div>
    <div>
      <p class="open-source-copy">Trustpoint is available as open-source software under the MIT license. You can explore, use and contribute to the project without purchasing commercial services from Trustpoint Labs.</p>
      <p class="open-source-copy">Trustpoint Labs is a commercial services partner supporting the adoption and professional use of Trustpoint. We provide Trustpoint-focused engineering, integration, custom development and contract-based support, while the open-source project remains distinct from our commercial offerings.</p>
      <div class="open-source-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project/trustpoint" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Trustpoint on GitHub <span>↗︎</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


      <!-- =================================
           CONTACT
      ================================== -->

      <section
        class="contact section"
        id="contact"
      >

        <div class="shell">

          <div class="section-label">
            <span class="square"></span>
            GET IN TOUCH
          </div>

          <div class="contact-grid">

            <div class="contact-copy">

              <h2>
                              Let's make Trustpoint work
              in your environment.
              </h2>

              <p class="lede">
                Tell us about your Trustpoint deployment, integration, custom engineering or support requirements.
              </p>

              <div class="contact-next">

                <h3>
                  Start with the right scope.
                </h3>

                <p>
                  We can start with a Trustpoint-focused technical workshop,
                  integration sprint or pilot deployment.
                  Early-stage requirements are welcome.
                </p>

              </div>

              <p class="contact-email">
                Prefer email?

                <a href="mailto:trustpoint@campus-schwarzwald.de">
                  trustpoint@campus-schwarzwald.de ↗︎
                </a>
              </p>

            </div>


            <div class="contact-panel">

              <h3>
                Discuss your Trustpoint project
              </h3>

              <p class="contact-note">
                Fields marked * are required.
              </p>

              <form
                name="contact"
                method="POST"
                action="/success/"
                data-netlify="true"
                class="contact-form"
              >

                <input
                  type="hidden"
                  name="form-name"
                  value="contact"
                />

                <label>
                  Name *

                  <input
                    type="text"
                    name="name"
                    autocomplete="name"
                    placeholder="Your name"
                    required
                  />
                </label>

                <label>
                  Work email *

                  <input
                    type="email"
                    name="email"
                    autocomplete="email"
                    placeholder="you@company.com"
                    required
                  />
                </label>

                <label>
                  Company *

                  <input
                    type="text"
                    name="company"
                    autocomplete="organization"
                    placeholder="Company or organization"
                    required
                  />
                </label>

                <label>
                  What would you like to achieve? *

                  <textarea
                    name="message"
                    rows="5"
                    placeholder="Trustpoint deployment, devices, integration or support requirements"
                    required
                  ></textarea>
                </label>

                <label>
                  Number of devices

                  <input
                    type="text"
                    name="devices"
                    placeholder="e.g. 25, 500, 5,000+"
                  />
                </label>

                <label>
                  Deployment environment

                  <input
                    type="text"
                    name="deployment"
                    placeholder="e.g. factory OT, edge appliance, isolated network"
                  />
                </label>

                <button
                  class="contact-submit"
                  type="submit"
                >
                  <span>Send inquiry</span>
                  <span aria-hidden="true">→︎</span>
                </button>

              </form>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- =================================
           FAQ
      ================================== -->

      <section class="faq section shell" aria-labelledby="faq-label">
  <div class="section-label" id="faq-label">A FEW PRACTICAL DETAILS</div>
  <div class="faq-layout">
    <h2>Good to know.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>What does Trustpoint Labs offer?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Trustpoint Labs provides engineering and integration, custom development, contract-based technical support and OEM/white-label services around the Trustpoint open-source platform.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is Trustpoint Labs the same as the Trustpoint project?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Trustpoint is an open-source software project. Trustpoint Labs is a commercial services partner offering professional assistance with adoption, deployment and integration.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to replace my existing PKI to use Trustpoint?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Not necessarily. Trustpoint can be integrated with existing issuing PKI infrastructure through supported interfaces and appropriate deployment modes. The architecture depends on your PKI, devices and network requirements.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you offer general PKI consulting without Trustpoint?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Our consulting and engineering offering focuses on deploying Trustpoint in industrial PKI and OT environments. We assess connected PKI systems and devices as part of those projects.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Which protocols and interfaces are supported?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Trustpoint includes certificate management and enrollment interfaces such as CMP, EST, REST APIs and OPC UA GDS functionality. The exact capabilities depend on the Trustpoint release and connected devices.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can Trustpoint operate in isolated networks?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Trustpoint supports local deployments without permanent cloud access. For certificate issuance and renewal, a suitable CA must be reachable within the deployment's network constraints.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What is included in commercial support?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Standard support is a contract-based break/fix service for eligible official Trustpoint releases. It covers defined Trustpoint troubleshooting and defect analysis, not new deployment projects, custom development or third-party system support. See the <a href="/support/">Support page</a> for details.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

    </main>


    <!-- ===================================
         FOOTER
    ==================================== -->

    <footer>

      <div class="footer-inner shell">

        <a
          href="/"
          aria-label="Trustpoint Labs"
        >
          <img
            class="footer-logo"
            src={trustpointLogo}
            alt="Trustpoint Labs"
            width="180"
            height="101"
          />
        </a>


        <div class="footer-links">

          <a href="/engineering-integration/">Engineering &amp; Integration</a>
          <a href="/support/">Support</a>
          <a href="/use-cases/">Use Cases</a>

          <a href="#offering">
            Offering
          </a>

          <a
            href={githubUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub ↗︎
          </a>

          <a href="/imprint">
            Imprint
          </a>

          <a href="/privacy">
            Privacy
          </a>

        </div>

      </div>

    </footer>

  </body>
</html>